Satge 1 update:
Created two endpoints and tested them


stage 2 update:
Build a public lobby anyone can enter, and a locked door — even before you've hired the guard.
Add a public endpoint GET /public/info . No auth. Returns { "message": "Welcome stranger! This
info is public." } with status 200.
Add a protected endpoint GET /protected/profile . To reach it, a client must send their access token in the
Authorization header as Authorization: Bearer <token> .
Inside the route, extract the token from that header.
If the header is missing, malformed, or has no token, immediately return 401 with { "error": "Access
token required" } . (You're not verifying the token yet — just checking one was presented.)


